Dedupe the group-edit profile dropdown's fallback options.

GroupUserProfileForm.vue's profileOptionsWithFallback getter builds
"fallback" dropdown options for any profile_uri used in the group's user
table but not present in the master profilesList (getAllProfiles()). It
maps over every row of userProfiles -- one row per user in the group -- and
filters against the known profile URIs, but never dedupes within the
fallback set itself. When a profile_uri shared by multiple users in the
group falls into this fallback branch, every user row referencing it
produces its own identical {value, text} option, so the dropdown renders
that profile's label once per user sharing it instead of once total
(confirmed on prod: 4 duplicate "Researcher profile" entries == 4 users in
the researchers group, all pointing at a valid, non-orphaned profile URI).
Upstream bug, present in 1.5.4, unfixed on develop 2026-09-16.

--- a/opensilex-front/front/src/components/groups/GroupUserProfileForm.vue
+++ b/opensilex-front/front/src/components/groups/GroupUserProfileForm.vue
@@ -136,15 +136,17 @@
     const knownProfileUris = new Set(
       existingOptions.map(option => option.value)
     );

-    const missingOptions = (this.userProfiles || [])
-      .map(userProfile => ({
-        value: userProfile.profile_uri,
-        text: userProfile.profile_name || userProfile.profile_uri
-      }))
-      .filter(option =>
-        option.value && !knownProfileUris.has(option.value)
-      );
+    const missingOptionsMap = new Map<string, { value: string; text: string }>();
+    (this.userProfiles || []).forEach(userProfile => {
+      if (userProfile.profile_uri && !knownProfileUris.has(userProfile.profile_uri)) {
+        missingOptionsMap.set(userProfile.profile_uri, {
+          value: userProfile.profile_uri,
+          text: userProfile.profile_name || userProfile.profile_uri
+        });
+      }
+    });
+    const missingOptions = [...missingOptionsMap.values()];

     return [...missingOptions, ...existingOptions];
   }
